# mutates: BUG-019 on the roll-FORWARD path, which is worse than the rollback one: a commit can be issued by a RESOLVER acting on somebody else's behalf, so the lock it steals belongs to a transaction that is not even a party to the operation. Same consequence -- an orphaned committed version -- and the same single detector
--- a/kv/txn.go
